00:10:29,211 --> 00:10:31,088
It was sort of on and off.
He'd come and go.

237
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:32,924
He'd mainly live with his parents, but...

238
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:35,176
then we broke up,
so whatever. [scoffs]

239
00:10:35,259 --> 00:10:37,219
Oh, um, I'm so sorry.

240
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:40,431
Don't be. I'm so glad we broke up...

241
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:42,767
I just don't really wanna live alone,
you know?

242
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:45,061
Well, that's perfect.
We can hang out.

243
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:46,562
And we will.

244
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:50,482
I just wanna really clearly establish
the roommate boundaries initially.

245
00:10:50,566 --> 00:10:52,193
[stuttering] Yeah. Yeah.

246
00:10:52,276 --> 00:10:54,528
That actually sounds like
we've got a lot in common.

247
00:10:56,823 --> 00:10:58,991
Well... [smacks lips]

248
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:01,368
get out of my space! [chuckles]

249
00:11:01,452 --> 00:11:03,162
This is gonna be fun.

250
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:38,114
But, Mother,
why is the wolf following me?

251
00:11:38,197 --> 00:11:40,491
Do not fear him.
He is your protector.

252
00:11:40,574 --> 00:11:43,535
Now that you're becoming a woman,
your powers are growing.

253
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:46,455
My powers? Am I becoming a witch?

254
00:11:46,538 --> 00:11:47,706
We will know soon enough.

255
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:49,876
When your body aligns
with the lunar cycle.

256
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:51,668
Now, command the wolf.

257
00:11:51,753 --> 00:11:54,713
-[inhales sharply]
-Sabien, submit.

258
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:02,096
He's not even looking at me.

259
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:03,347
Uh, cut!

260
00:12:03,430 --> 00:12:06,017
All right, let's get the wolf to sit.
How about that? What's the problem?

261
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:10,062
Arya, you have to make your hand a fist
or the wolf won't sit.

262
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:11,188
I was.

263
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:13,190
No, actually, you were just
holding your hand up.

264
00:12:13,274 --> 00:12:14,441
Are you blind or something?

265
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:17,361
I was doing exactly what you said to.
The dog's just stupid.

266
00:12:17,444 --> 00:12:20,031
God, just check the playback,
I was doing it.

267
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:21,866
Arya, superstar, what up?

268
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:23,284
[groaning] I'm so tired!

269
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:27,079
-Evan.
-Hey, what's up, man?

270
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,998
Hey, man. What's going on?

271
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:31,208
Not much.
What do you need?

272
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,460
-Tutor time.
-Seriously? You're doing this now?

273
00:12:33,544 --> 00:12:36,380
Dude, have you been paying attention?
We lose the wolf in half an hour.

274
00:12:36,463 --> 00:12:38,424
No, I get it. I just... you know...

275
00:12:38,507 --> 00:12:40,426
Arya needs her three hours of class...

276
00:12:40,509 --> 00:12:41,635
-every day.
-Right.

277
00:12:41,718 --> 00:12:44,555
I'm dealing with a child actor
and a live animal here.

278
00:12:44,638 --> 00:12:46,098
I-- I just need you to be a team player.

279
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,892
I know. But I feel like it's always

280
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:50,394
animals that are coming in and push,
you know...

281
00:12:50,477 --> 00:12:51,770
One day it's snakes,
the next day it's--

282
00:12:51,854 --> 00:12:54,065
Dude, have you ever worked
on a supernatural period piece before?

283
00:12:54,148 --> 00:12:57,568
Come on, man. Everyday there's
a serpent or there's a mule.

284
00:12:57,651 --> 00:12:59,320
I'm looking out for Arya here, okay?

285
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:02,531
I don't know what to tell you, man.
They're witches, they deal with animals.

286
00:13:02,614 --> 00:13:05,284
Evan, she needs three hours
of class every day, okay?

287
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:06,368
So we're doing this.

288
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:08,370
Seriously?
That's the tone you're gonna take?

289
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:10,289
Yeah, come on, man.
It's the law.

290
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:11,790
-It's called working--
-What's going on?

291
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:14,251
-Is there an issue?
-Susan, hey.

292
00:13:14,335 --> 00:13:15,962
Uh, no issues.

293
00:13:16,045 --> 00:13:17,421
Lovin' the scene, it's so good.

294
00:13:17,504 --> 00:13:19,465
Guys, this wolf is almost out the door.

295
00:13:19,548 --> 00:13:20,842
-Can we handle this some other time?
-[Evan] Yes.

296
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:22,009
Right, but it's just--

297
00:13:22,093 --> 00:13:23,135
If Arya's not in class

298
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:24,929
and somebody reports this,
we could lose our jobs and--

299
00:13:25,012 --> 00:13:26,555
[scoffs] Dude, you are the only one
that cares about--

300
00:13:26,638 --> 00:13:27,764
But we could.
We could lose our jobs!

301
00:13:27,849 --> 00:13:29,934
Hey, hey, hey.
Why are we going crazy here?

302
00:13:30,017 --> 00:13:32,019
Gus, listen.

303
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:34,730
I respect your passion
and commitment here.

304
00:13:34,813 --> 00:13:36,607
-Thank you. Thank you.
-[Susan] You know?

305
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:38,192
Yeah, and, you know,
and if the wolf goes away

306
00:13:38,275 --> 00:13:40,277
before we get this shot,
you know, that's... that's fine.

307
00:13:40,361 --> 00:13:41,904
You know, we'll... we'll work it out.

308
00:13:41,988 --> 00:13:44,115
That means so much.
I appreciate that. Thank you.

309
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:45,992
What would that mean, Evan?

310
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:48,119
I'm guessing we just have to
come in on Saturday to finish?

311
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:49,203
Uh-huh. Yeah.

312
00:13:49,286 --> 00:13:50,787
Yeah, just come in over the weekend.

313
00:13:50,872 --> 00:13:51,873
-Yep. Mmm-hmm.
-Mmm.

314
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:53,875
The crew will probably not like that much.

315
00:13:53,958 --> 00:13:55,542
[Evan] Oh, they're gonna be pissed.

316
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:56,878
I mean, I guess
you don't give a fuck about

317
00:13:56,961 --> 00:13:59,171
people spending time with their kids.
Oh, wait, you don't have kids.

318
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,339
-[Evan] That's for sure.
-Uh...

319
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:03,425
I feel like we're wasting time
by arguing about it, so...

320
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:04,801
[inhales] Let's just do it.

321
00:14:04,886 --> 00:14:06,637
-Really? Excellent.
-[Gus] We'll do it. Mmm-hmm.

322
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:07,721
You're my soldier.

323
00:14:07,804 --> 00:14:10,016
All right, we got another take,
everybody. Second take.

324
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:12,559
Uh, why does everyone else get a CGI wolf?

325
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:14,186
Why the fuck do we have a real wolf here?

326
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:16,772
Arya, hey. False alarm.

327
00:14:16,855 --> 00:14:19,775
It's gonna be about 50 more minutes.
And then, we'll take it to class.

328
00:14:19,858 --> 00:14:21,110
I can't. I need a nap.

329
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:22,904
[clicks tongue] Nope. No naps today.

330
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:26,032
-I've been here since 6:00.
-I know that.

331
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:27,699
But how you gonna count
all that money you got if,

332
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:29,451
uh, you don't know math, right?

333
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:32,413
Um, Jeff, the accountant?

334
00:14:32,496 --> 00:14:33,747
Right, Jeff.

335
00:14:33,830 --> 00:14:36,417
He's an Orthodox Jew,
I think he knows what he's doing.

336
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:37,709
Oh.

337
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:39,962
[hip-hop music playing on car speakers]

338
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:50,973
[man on radio] Our next caller
is Jason from Chicago.

339
00:14:51,057 --> 00:14:54,018
Jason, how we doin'?
How's our day going?

340
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:55,727
[Jason] Well, my mom passed away.

341
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:57,688
Oh. My condolences.

342
00:14:57,771 --> 00:15:00,191
I have to say,
I'm not too torn up about it,

343
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:02,901
and actually, that's
what's kind of got me upset.

344
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:04,861
The fact that I'm not upset.

345
00:15:04,946 --> 00:15:06,989
We can't control how we feel.

346
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:09,533
And sometimes... [inhales]

347
00:15:09,616 --> 00:15:13,245
these archetypical people in our lives,
they hurt us.

348
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:16,373
And they don't fulfill the archetype.

349
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,584
What... what's an archetype?

350
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:20,627
An archetype is a...

351
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:23,422
Well, I don't really have
the exact definition.

352
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:26,717
I do know what it means, obviously,
because I just used it. Um...

353
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,469
-[inhales]
-[radio show theme music playing]

354
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:30,512
Well, thank you so much for calling.

355
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:31,722
I am Dr. Greg Coulter

356
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:35,017
and you are listening
to the Love and Living Channel

357
00:15:35,101 --> 00:15:37,061
on Gravity Satellite Radio.

358
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:39,771
You listen, we hear.

359
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:43,067
Great. Great show, Greg.

360
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:44,443
[Dr. Greg] Oh, thanks so much, Rob.

361
00:15:44,526 --> 00:15:46,028
-I really appreciate it.
-So good.

362
00:15:46,112 --> 00:15:47,821
-Good morning, Mickey.
-Hey, you said you wanted to talk?

363
00:15:47,904 --> 00:15:48,905
Yeah.

364
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:51,867
We need to fire Rob. Rob's gotta go.
Does that make me evil?

365
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:54,036
No! Please. This is a business.

366
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,912
You know what?

367
00:15:55,997 --> 00:15:57,789
Can you fire him for me... huh?

368
00:15:57,873 --> 00:16:00,001
-Or do program managers not do that?
-[sighs]

369
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:01,918
What? I mean, okay,
you know what? I'll do it.

370
00:16:02,003 --> 00:16:03,504
If you do it, Rob will think I'm a coward.

371
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:05,089
Yeah, I think that's probably
the right move.

372
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:06,632
No, wait, you know what?
You do it.

373
00:16:06,715 --> 00:16:08,175
I'm sorry, I'll stop being annoying.

374
00:16:09,176 --> 00:16:11,220
So what's the problem?
What did he do?

375
00:16:11,303 --> 00:16:14,723
Look... Rob does a great job...

376
00:16:14,806 --> 00:16:16,642
but the guy creeps me out.

377
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:18,894
He's got this look in his eyes.
You ever meet a person

378
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:20,729
and they smile, and you feel like
they're screaming at you?

379
00:16:20,812 --> 00:16:22,064
What? Rob?

380
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:24,108
Rob's like the nicest guy
in the whole world.

381
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:25,692
He's nicer than both of us.

382
00:16:25,776 --> 00:16:30,114
Well, he's just got this bad energy,
this aura around him.

383
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:32,574
Has he ever done anything to you?

384
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:34,535
He asked me do I like him.

385
00:16:36,287 --> 00:16:39,498
That's weird, right?
That's not a thing you ask anybody.

386
00:16:39,581 --> 00:16:42,334
-Let alone in a workplace.
-[sighs]

387
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:46,797
Look... I would fire him
but I can't take that on right now.

388
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:49,216
This might be a difficult thing
for you to understand

389
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:51,218
but I am very vulnerable in this job.

390
00:16:51,302 --> 00:16:52,553
I have to be.

391
00:16:52,636 --> 00:16:55,139
I make myself vulnerable to the world.

392
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:58,016
I can't be vulnerable
around somebody like Rob.

393
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,143
So he's gotta go.

394
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:01,978
Fine, I'll do it just
to end this conversation.

395
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,106
I'm a pussy, aren't I?

396
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:05,441
I'm sorry, I'm disgusting.

397
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:07,859
Okay, you know what? I'll do it.

398
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:09,778
-[whispers] Thank you.
-Oh, question.

399
00:17:09,861 --> 00:17:13,240
What is a good band to work out to?
Something new.

400
00:17:13,324 --> 00:17:15,451
[exhales] I don't know. The Monkees?

401
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:17,244
That's great. [chuckles]

402
00:17:17,328 --> 00:17:19,288
Thanks, you're the best.
You know what?

403
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:20,581
You fire Rob.

404
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:24,876
[woman] So how was the move
out of the Springwood?

405
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:28,922
Uh, you know, it's funny
it didn't end up actually happening.

406
00:17:29,005 --> 00:17:30,966
He finally realizes
that the Springwood rules.

407
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:32,843
You love it there, right?

408
00:17:34,095 --> 00:17:37,223
No. I mean... not exactly.

409
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:38,599
You can live anywhere in LA!

410
00:17:38,682 --> 00:17:40,184
Okay, like, where?

411
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:41,935
I mean... [stutters] I've been looking,
but it's just...

412
00:17:42,018 --> 00:17:44,480
I'm having a hard time
finding a place I like.

413
00:17:44,563 --> 00:17:46,357
You can move near me.
The Eastside.

414
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:49,568
I don't know.
It's just a little too cool. And now...

415
00:17:49,651 --> 00:17:52,738
I'd be like the Beverly Hills guy with,
like, a white Corvette.

416
00:17:55,116 --> 00:17:56,992
[clears throat] I mean,
is that what we're doing?

417
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,870
[stammers] We're just playing
what we'd wanna be?

418
00:17:59,953 --> 00:18:02,706
I don't think it's, like,
what I want to be. It's, like, who I am.

419
00:18:02,789 --> 00:18:04,082
Like, who am I?

420
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:06,377
I mean, like, where do guys
like me live, you know?

421
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:09,713
Where do the, like,
repressed hostile nerds

422
00:18:09,796 --> 00:18:13,925
whose girlfriend's accuse them
of being "fake nice" live?

423
00:18:14,009 --> 00:18:15,969
-Santa Monica?
-No.

424
00:18:16,052 --> 00:18:18,347
As long as I stay in the Springwood,
you know...

425
00:18:18,430 --> 00:18:22,476
maybe I get a text from Natalie saying,
"Let's try it again."

426
00:18:22,559 --> 00:18:25,521
And I can just bop out of the Springwood
back to another place

427
00:18:25,604 --> 00:18:29,566
instead of like, bop Springwood,
bop new place, bop Natalie.

428
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:30,901
It's crazy, right?

429
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:34,113
Please don't tell me you think you
and Natalie are gonna get back together.

430
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:36,865
-'Cause that's never gonna happen.
-Yeah.

431
00:18:36,948 --> 00:18:39,576
You're saying it... like, it's over?

432
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,703
She cheated on you.
Why would you wanna be with her?

433
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:43,414
Gus, she sucked, man.

434
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:46,125
[woman] Fuck Natalie.
And fuck the Springwood.

435
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:47,501
I think you'll find someone better.

436
00:18:47,584 --> 00:18:49,586
[stammers] You know,
I know you'll find someone better

437
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:51,630
and if you have trouble,
I can set you up.

438
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:53,048
She wasn't right for you, dude.

439
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:54,383
I think I gotta go.

440
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:56,968
Gus. Wait. We gotta...

441
00:18:57,886 --> 00:18:59,095
[sighs] We gotta pay.

442
00:19:00,972 --> 00:19:05,269
Otis, put the dirt down now!

443
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:06,478
I suppose it's better than Heather's kid.

444
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:07,813
-She eats dog shit.
-[snorts]

445
00:19:07,896 --> 00:19:09,690
[laughs] I'm serious.

446
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:13,860
Oh, my God, this day is dragging.

447
00:19:14,861 --> 00:19:16,822
You know what
my favorite part of the day is?

448
00:19:16,905 --> 00:19:18,615
[sighs] Taking my Ambien.

449
00:19:18,699 --> 00:19:20,492
-Really?
-Yeah.

450
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:22,619
There's this moment
right after it kicks in,

451
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:26,081
and I'm still awake
and everything is perfect.

452
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:28,709
Seriously, I look forward
to 9:30 every day.

453
00:19:28,792 --> 00:19:30,669
I don't like that shit.

454
00:19:30,752 --> 00:19:32,879
I always wake up having made spaghetti.

455
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:36,049
[chuckling] Spaghetti is the best.
What's wrong with that?

456
00:19:36,132 --> 00:19:37,259
You want some Ambien?

457
00:19:37,343 --> 00:19:38,677
No, thanks. [sighs]

458
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:40,095
Are you sober?

459
00:19:40,178 --> 00:19:41,305
Kinda.

460
00:19:42,138 --> 00:19:43,307
I get it.

461
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,852
Fuck it! Give me some Ambien.

462
00:19:46,935 --> 00:19:48,979
Give me a whole handful.

463
00:19:49,062 --> 00:19:51,190
[inhales sharply] All right.

464
00:19:54,901 --> 00:19:57,153
I'm sure you have your own methods...

465
00:19:57,238 --> 00:19:58,989
but I turn off all electronic devices.

466
00:19:59,072 --> 00:20:01,867
The last time I took an Ambien,
I emailed my high school principal

467
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:04,077
to tell him what a great job he had done.

468
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:06,997
[chuckles softly] That's why
you're my favorite neighbor.

469
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,290
[chuckles]

470
00:20:08,374 --> 00:20:10,542
Otis, enough with the dirt.

471
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:12,669
You have reached your quota.

472
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:14,087
Down.

473
00:20:17,674 --> 00:20:19,426
[indistinct chatter]

474
00:20:22,804 --> 00:20:25,181
You know, I guess she used to be
an extra on The Little Rascals.

475
00:20:25,266 --> 00:20:26,308
For real?

476
00:20:26,392 --> 00:20:28,018
-Yeah, no, she told me that.
-[man] Jeez.

